rriable at all - the language official origin, the manager operator documentation, or this specification, all manager-trusted. Vectors 47, 48, 53.\n\n(3) Guidance lifecycle implementable. Grammar is toolchain.<id>.<reason>.<platform>.r<N>, N decimal starting at 1, strictly increasing per tuple. Published IDs immutable; a change of meaning/origin/class creates the next revision; superseded_by must name an existing same-tuple entry with a strictly greater revision, so the chain is acyclic; exactly one active entry per tuple; retired entries retained. Selection still resolves the tuple. Vectors 49, 50, 51, 52.\n\n(4) Channel contradiction resolved by surface, not by field type. New reference 3.1: on the manager-defined wire surface the field set is closed, no channel field exists and any such value is forbidden; on the source-ecosystem metadata surface each entry declares a closed disposition table (forbidden/compared/ignored) where forbidden is reserved for values naming WHERE a toolchain comes from and channel/track values are compared. Fixed precedence: forbidden fields evaluated before compared, Unicode-scalar order of source path then field path, so path plus nightly is always package_influence_forbidden. Channel classification is deterministic: version literal = at_least assertion; stable = permitted and never honored (deliberate relaxation - it asserts exactly the release-only property v1 enforces); beta/nightly/dated = mismatch; anything else = mismatch. Stage B classification vectors take the resolved version as fixture input, so reserved-toolchain cases need no host. Vectors 10, 11, 35-42.\n\n(5) Cache vector corrected. Old vector 35 removed. Reference 4.3 and decision section 6 now state two distinct rows: an incompatible current toolchain fails at Stage A with cache lookup never reached, no candidate consulted, no rebuild, no mutation; a cache candidate carrying a different toolchain identity under a compatible current toolchain is an ordinary key miss and rebuild. Replaced by positive 14 and negative 45.\n\nVector inventory 40 -> 58 cases. Decision gained five rejected alternatives (requirement-only admissibility, package-reachable family set, blanket channel prohibition, tuple-only guidance IDs, host-only guidance reasons) and states that no currently admitted Go release becomes inadmissible and none currently rejected becomes admissible.\n\nGates, standalone, real exit codes: validate 0 (42 schemas / 422 vector files), python unittest 0 (29 tests), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0 no output, git diff --check 0, generate-vectors 0. Regenerated conformance/v1 and release/1.0.0-rc.5.json byte-identical to the accepted predecessor. Clean git-init probe at 1b02fa0: regenerate-check x2 = 0, release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5 = 0. Two negative probes against the reworked files expected-red and red: retired descriptor stem rejected by validate (exit 1), broken local link rejected by validate (exit 1); both reverted, final validate 0. make regenerate-check still cannot pass inside the task worktree because it diffs against 57c1f56 with the rc.5 candidate uncommitted - determinism proven by predecessor byte-comparison and the clean probe instead. Python gates run with the existing validation-venv because ambient python3 lacks jsonschema.\n\nReviewer focus for this cycle: does compatibility fully restore manager.md 2.2 and is requirement-before-compatibility the right precedence; is the 3.1 surface split a real distinction rather than a relabeling; is channel=stable permitted rather than mismatched correct (the one place this cycle relaxes previous text); do the identity code-to-reason mapping and guidance_class keep primary_source honest for authoring/configuration reasons; is the revisioned ID plus one-active-per-tuple sufficient for TASK-260728-ypbuav; does splitting old vector 35 into positive 14 and negative 45 leave any cache-versus-fail-fast case unstated.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-e41666, pid=17140, exit=0)\nReview cycle 2 focus: independently verify each prior blocking finding is closed, not merely restated. In particular, Go 1.99 must fail the manager-owned exact tested-family compatibility predicate despite satisfying at_least; pre-baseline precedence must be deterministic; all 12 diagnostics must have a total valid guidance mapping; revisioned guidance IDs must permit immutable supersession and one active tuple; invalid declared ids must still resolve guidance safely; manifest/descriptor channels remain forbidden while source metadata compared fields can never select/activate a toolchain and forbidden fields win; current incompatibility never reaches cache while differing compatible toolchain identity is a miss/rebuild. Challenge whether stable source channel acceptance and guidance primary-source classes preserve trust. Re-run unchanged rc.5, deterministic, link, retired-name and release gates. No edits, stage, commit, publish, pin or platform claim by reviewer.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-092e80, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-092e80)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-092e80, pid=29455, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 2 directive 2026-07-28: queued for the first free Claude Opus 5 producer slot; continue only in the existing task-owned curator-spec worktree and preserve the accepted predecessor read-only. Close all four cycle-2 blockers from TASK-260728-1g0z69_review-verdict-cycle-2.md: (1) make the complete Go metadata classifier exhaustive over every officially admitted ToolchainName class, including toolchain default, canonical release names, and custom/non-canonical names, with deterministic outcomes and focused vectors; (2) partition or explicitly order overlapping wire invalid-vs-package-influence and Stage-A unavailable-vs-untrusted triggers, with overlap vectors; (3) define a representable typed diagnostic payload union/optionality for invalid and empty-intersection requirements, including retained validated source fragments and payload-shape vectors; (4) define allowed guidance coverage modes, exact-OS plus any fallback behavior, and append-only/cross-version retirement transitions, with hybrid and transition vectors. Preserve the twelve-code totality, tested-family gate, revisioned IDs, source-metadata disposition split, cache ordering, all rc.5 bytes, and the previous five accepted fixes. No schema/release/pin/commit/staging change; rerun deterministic and unchanged-rc.5 gates, attach a new rework artifact, and hand off to a new independent reviewer cycle.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-1ccd8b, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-1ccd8b)\nRework cycle 2 complete: all four cycle-2 blocking findings closed in the same task worktree /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1g0z69/curator-spec-worktree. Delta versus the accepted predecessor is still exactly decisions/0007-compiled-build-toolchain-preflight.md, docs/compiled-build-toolchain-requirements.md and one CHANGELOG bullet. Nothing staged, committed, published, pinned; no platform validation claimed. Predecessor worktree preserved read-only.\n\n(1) Go classifier exhaustive. New reference 4.2.1-4.2.4. One shared goVersionLiteral grammar yielding a base triple plus prerelease flag. The go directive has 4 total classes and NO forbidden class - a value with a path separator is unclassifiable, not package influence, stated explicitly. The toolchain directive has 7 total ordered classes: path-bearing and custom-distribution (go1.23.4-bigcorp) are forbidden, default is permitted and never honored, canonical release and prerelease names compare by base triple, catch-all is mismatch; a repeated directive is the catch-all. Base-triple canonicalization is exact rather than approximate: Go orders 1.21 < 1.21rc1 < 1.21.0, and the two orders can differ only for a comparand strictly between a language version and its release, every such value being a prerelease that Stage A already rejected. go.work is deliberately not a metadata source because protocol/core.md 4.2 fixes GOWORK=off. Grammar taken from on-host primary sources (modfile ToolchainRE/GoVersionRE, gover.FromToolchain), not from memory. Supporting rule: new 3.1.1 value classifiers for a field whose value space spans dispositions - ordered classes, forbidden first, mandatory catch-all.\n\n(2) Overlapping triggers partitioned, not ordered. Wire surface: unknown key is the existing unknown-field schema rejection, malformed value is build_toolchain_requirement_invalid, so package_influence_forbidden never fires on the wire and is a Stage B code only. Rationale: classifying a malformed literal as smuggled influence requires inferring intent from a byte string and two managers would infer differently. The field-addition prohibition moves to a release gate over published schema property names, owned by TASK-260728-2jaw7h, because a field that does not exist produces no value to diagnose. Stage A step 2 splits into 2a declaration / 2b origin trust / 2c shape: unavailable means nothing was declared and is produced only by 2a; untrusted means something was declared and is unusable, including a declared root that does not exist. The cut is declaration presence, not severity, and it matches the existing guidance classes (host vs configuration).\n\n(3) Payload representable. New 5.1: a discriminated union whose shape is derived, not chosen - a code carries exactly the values established where it fires, and the stage steps are totally ordered, so shape is a function of the code. effective_requirement absent in exactly two codes, resolved_version and prerelease absent in exactly five. requirement_invalid carries source_ref plus a closed violation token and must not echo the offending value (no unvalidated package byte in a payload); requirement_unsatisfiable carries the individually validated fragments plus the max-lower and min-upper bounds with every source achieving each in fixed order, so the payload is as source-order-independent as the intersection.\n\n(4) Catalog unambiguous. Coverage is defined by the selection function: any, per_os and hybrid are all valid, and the gate checks resolution (every registry OS resolves to exactly one active entry) plus reachability (an exact entry for an OS outside the registry, or an any entry shadowed everywhere, fails). New 6.2.1 states append-only against the catalog version: a published version is immutable in whole, every change is an N to N+1 transition, the entry set only grows, active and superseded_by are one-way monotone, and four transitions are admissible including retire-without-successor only for a tuple the gate no longer requires. Exactly-one-active-per-tuple relaxes to at-most-one.\n\nVector inventory 58 -> 95 cases: Go classifier positives 9/10/12/13/14 and negatives 45-54 including class boundary 47 and value-class precedence 54; overlap vectors 24-28 and 33-34; payload-shape vectors 65-71; catalog coverage 79-84 and version transitions 85-90. Decision 0007 gained eight rejected alternatives.\n\nGates, standalone, real exit codes: validate 0 (42 schemas / 422 vector files), python unittest 0 (29 tests), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0 no output, git diff --check 0, generate-vectors 0. Regenerated conformance/v1 and release/1.0.0-rc.5.json byte-identical to the accepted predecessor. Clean git-init probe clean-probe-c2 at 773147f: regenerate-check x2 = 0, release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5 = 0. Two negative probes against the reworked files expected-red and red: retired descriptor stem rejected by validate (exit 1), broken local link rejected by validate (exit 1); both reverted, final validate 0 and both files byte-identical to their pre-probe copies. make regenerate-check still cannot pass inside the task worktree because it diffs against 57c1f56 with the rc.5 candidate uncommitted - determinism proven by predecessor byte-comparison and the clean probe. Python gates use the existing validation-venv because ambient python3 lacks jsonschema.\n\nReviewer focus: is the wire partition airtight in both directions; does 2a-2c leave any resolution failure unclassified; are the seven toolchain classes exhaustive over upstream grammar and is custom-distribution-as-package-influence right versus mismatch; does the base-triple equivalence hold for every Stage B comparison including short literals Curator admits but Go rejects; is payload shape a function of the code for all twelve and does no-echo leave any diagnostic under-informative; do resolution plus reachability fully replace the coverage-mode question and do the four version transitions cover every real catalog edit.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-1ccd8b, pid=42374, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 3 directive 2026-07-28: independently verify the four cycle-2 findings on the final rework, not merely its green gates. Challenge the total Go metadata classifier against official ToolchainName grammar, including default, canonical releases/prereleases, custom distributions, path-bearing and unclassifiable names; confirm deterministic outcomes and no package selector is honored. Verify wire invalid-vs-Stage-B package-influence and Stag