ying a different toolchain identity under a compatible current toolchain is an ordinary key miss and rebuild. Replaced by positive 14 and negative 45.\n\nVector inventory 40 -\u003e 58 cases. Decision gained five rejected alternatives (requirement-only admissibility, package-reachable family set, blanket channel prohibition, tuple-only guidance IDs, host-only guidance reasons) and states that no currently admitted Go release becomes inadmissible and none currently rejected becomes admissible.\n\nGates, standalone, real exit codes: validate 0 (42 schemas / 422 vector files), python unittest 0 (29 tests), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0 no output, git diff --check 0, generate-vectors 0. Regenerated conformance/v1 and release/1.0.0-rc.5.json byte-identical to the accepted predecessor. Clean git-init probe at 1b02fa0: regenerate-check x2 = 0, release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5 = 0. Two negative probes against the reworked files expected-red and red: retired descriptor stem rejected by validate (exit 1), broken local link rejected by validate (exit 1); both reverted, final validate 0. make regenerate-check still cannot pass inside the task worktree because it diffs against 57c1f56 with the rc.5 candidate uncommitted - determinism proven by predecessor byte-comparison and the clean probe instead. Python gates run with the existing validation-venv because ambient python3 lacks jsonschema.\n\nReviewer focus for this cycle: does compatibility fully restore manager.md 2.2 and is requirement-before-compatibility the right precedence; is the 3.1 surface split a real distinction rather than a relabeling; is channel=stable permitted rather than mismatched correct (the one place this cycle relaxes previous text); do the identity code-to-reason mapping and guidance_class keep primary_source honest for authoring/configuration reasons; is the revisioned ID plus one-active-per-tuple sufficient for TASK-260728-ypbuav; does splitting old vector 35 into positive 14 and negative 45 leave any c