ead-only.\n\n(1) Go classifier exhaustive. New reference 4.2.1-4.2.4. One shared goVersionLiteral grammar yielding a base triple plus prerelease flag. The go directive has 4 total classes and NO forbidden class - a value with a path separator is unclassifiable, not package influence, stated explicitly. The toolchain directive has 7 total ordered classes: path-bearing and custom-distribution (go1.23.4-bigcorp) are forbidden, default is permitted and never honored, canonical release and prerelease names compare by base triple, catch-all is mismatch; a repeated directive is the catch-all. Base-triple canonicalization is exact rather than approximate: Go orders 1.21 \u003c 1.21rc1 \u003c 1.21.0, and the two orders can differ only for a comparand strictly between a language version and its release, every such value being a prerelease that Stage A already rejected. go.work is deliberately not a metadata source because protocol/core.md 4.2 fixes GOWORK=off. Grammar taken from on-host primary sources (modfile ToolchainRE/GoVersionRE, gover.FromToolchain), not from memory. Supporting rule: new 3.1.1 value classifiers for a field whose value space spans dispositions - ordered classes, forbidden first, mandatory catch-all.\n\n(2) Overlapping triggers partitioned, not ordered. Wire surface: unknown key is the existing unknown-field schema rejection, malformed value is build_toolchain_requirement_invalid, so package_influence_forbidden never fires on the wire and is a Stage B code only. Rationale: classifying a malformed literal as smuggled influence requires inferring intent from a byte string and two managers would infer differently. The field-addition prohibition moves to a release gate over published schema property names, owned by TASK-260728-2jaw7h, because a field that does not exist produces no value to diagnose. Stage A step 2 splits into 2a declaration / 2b origin trust / 2c shape: unavailable means nothing was declared and is produced only by 2a; untrusted means something was declared and is unusable, including a declared root that does not exist. The cut is declaration presence, not severity, and it matches the existing guidance classes (host vs configuration).\n\n(3) Payload representable. New 5.1: a discriminated union whose shape is derived, not chosen - a code carries exactly the values established where it fires, and the stage steps are totally ordered, so shape is a function of the code. effective_requirement absent in exactly two codes, resolved_version and prerelease absent in exactly five. requirement_invalid carries source_ref plus a closed violation token and must not echo the offending value (no unvalidated package byte in a payload); requirement_unsatisfiable carries the individually validated fragments plus the max-lower and min-upper bounds with every source achieving each in fixed order, so the payload is as source-order-independent as the intersection.\n\n(4) Catalog unambiguous. Coverage is defined by the selection function: any, per_os and hybrid are all valid, and the gate checks resolution (every registry OS resolves to exactly one active entry) plus reachability (an exact entry for an OS outside the registry, or an any entry shadowed everywhere, fails). New 6.2.1 states append-only against the catalog version: a published version is immutable in whole, every change is an N to N+1 transition, the entry set only grows, active and superseded_by are one-way monotone, and four transitions are admissible including retire-without-successor only for a tuple the gate no longer requires. Exactly-one-active-per-tuple relaxes to at-most-one.\n\nVector inventory 58 -\u003e 95 cases: Go classifier positives 9/10/12/13/14 and negatives 45-54 including class boundary 47 and value-class precedence 54; overlap vectors 24-28 and 33-34; payload-shape vectors 65-71; catalog coverage 79-84 and version transitions 85-90. Decision 0007 gained eight rejected alternatives.\n\nGates, standalone, real exit codes: validate 0 (42 schemas / 422 vector files), python unittest 0 (29 tests), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0 no output, git diff --check 0, generate-vectors 0. Regenerated conformance/v1 and release/1.0.0-rc.5.json byte-identical to the accepted predecessor. Clean git-init probe clean-probe-c2 at 773147f: regenerate-check x2 = 0, release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5 = 0. Two negative probes against the reworked files expected-red and red: retired descriptor stem rejected by validate (exit 1), broken local link rejected by validate (exit 1); both reverted, final validate 0 and both files byte-identical to their pre-probe copies. make regenerate-check still cannot pass inside the task worktree because it diffs against 57c1f56 with the rc.5 candidate uncommitted - determinism proven by predecessor byte-comparison and the clean probe. Python gates use the existing validation-venv because ambient python3 lacks jsonschema.\n\nReviewer focus: is the wire partition airtight in both directions; does 2a-2c leave any resolution failure unclassified; are the seven toolchain classes exhaustive over upstream grammar and is custom-distribution-as-package-influence right versus mismatch; does the base-triple equivalence hold for every Stage B comparison including short literals Curator admits but Go rejects; is payload shape a function of the code for all twelve and does no-echo leave any diagnostic under-informative; do resolution plus reachability fully replace the coverage-mode question and do the four version transitions cover every real catalog edit.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-1ccd8b, pid=42374, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 3 directive 2026-07-28: independently verify the four cycle-2 findings on the final rework, not merely its green gates. Challenge the total Go metadata classifier against official ToolchainName grammar, including default, canonical releases/prereleases, custom distributions, path-bearing and unclassifiable names; confirm deterministic outcomes and no package selector is honored. Verify wire invalid-vs-Stage-B package-influence and Stage-A unavailable-vs-untrusted are disjoint by input, not overlapping by outcome. Verify diagnostic payload shapes are representable, deterministic, retain only validated fragments, and never echo unvalidated package bytes. Verify any/per_os/hybrid guidance coverage resolves every supported OS with no unreachable active entry and catalog N-to-N+1 retirement is monotone while published versions stay immutable. Confirm the 95-case normative inventory is complete for this design task, prior fixes remain intact, and all rc.5/schema/vector/release bytes remain unchanged. Re-run focused adversarial probes and deterministic/release gates; no edits, staging, commit, publication, pins or platform claims; attach explicit verdict and route status.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-0e6d1a, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-0e6d1a)\nReviewer cycle 3 verdict: changes requested. Evidence attached as TASK-260728-1g0z69_review-verdict-cycle-3.md. Route to analysis for four contract corrections: disjoint Stage-A declaration/origin triggers; an explicit Stage-B rejection when a late descriptor requirement excludes the resolved host; deterministic platform applicability before OS-specific resolution/probing; and a complete pre-compiler outcome for Go-invalid directive values/file shapes. All submitted non-mutating gates pass and frozen rc.5 bytes remain unchanged."}},{"ok":true,"result":{"primary":{"action":"status_changed","element_id":"TASK-260728-1g0z69","field":"status","new_value":"analysis","old_value":"reviewing"},"side_ef