   635	*Ground one — the process closure.* Under exec containment allowing only the
   636	curatable roots, a hello-world `-produce program -target macos_arm64` cannot
   637	run without host executables. Two iterative-denial runs were made. `run7`,
   638	seeded empty, established `/bin/bash` and `/usr/bin/xcrun` as required and its
   639	raw output additionally shows `/usr/bin/xcode-select`, `/usr/libexec/PlistBuddy`
   640	and `<Xcode>/Contents/Developer/usr/bin/xcodebuild` denied. `run8`, seeded with
   641	the first four, reached exit 0 after adding
   642	`<Xcode>/…/XcodeDefault.xctoolchain/usr/bin/ld` and `…/usr/bin/dsymutil`. So the
   643	**union observed** is seven and the set **sufficient** for a successful compile
   644	is **six**; `run8`'s final `allowed-externals.txt` correctly holds those six, and
   645	the difference is path-dependent because an allowed `xcode-select` removes the
   646	`xcrun xcodebuild -version` fallback. Revision 2 called the set "exactly seven",
   647	conflating the two; that claim is **withdrawn**.
   648	
   649	Iterative denial proves each listed executable is required on the path taken and
   650	that the listed set is sufficient. It does not prove that no other executable is
   651	spawned on any path, so **no completeness claim is made for macOS** — and none
   652	is needed. Decision 0008 section 6 item 3 is violated by the first external
   653	executable; `/bin/bash`, `/usr/bin/xcode-select`, `/usr/libexec/PlistBuddy` and
   654	`/usr/bin/xcrun` are absolute OS paths compiled into the compiler that no
   655	operator-curated root can contain; and ground two is independent of the process
   656	count. This asymmetry is why section 12's A3 now requires a **kernel-level trace
   657	that records every process start by resolved image path** for a tuple that is to
   658	be *admitted*: sufficiency is enough to exclude, only completeness is enough to
   659	qualify.
