notes:QUEUED EXECUTION DIRECTIVE 2026-07-28: Compare Kotlin/JVM versus Kotlin/Native as required by the task, but honor the product requirement that the compiled CLI driver target is Kotlin/Native unless evidence proves the accepted native-executable-v1 boundary cannot be met, in which case retire the identifiers explicitly rather than silently switching to JVM. Build from accepted TASK-260728-2spy93, TASK-260728-1g0z69 and TASK-260729-rhjxtx evidence. Select paired local/external identifiers, trusted Kotlin/Native root/konanc identity, version/target normalization, compatibility families, artifact and distribution layout, cache/receipt/marker identity, and fail-before-compiler ordering. There is no legal ecosystem manifest measured for pure metadata and Gradle scripts execute code: specify a neutral manager-owned metadata surface consistent with skill-build.json/local build_roots or fail closed; no generic Gradle/Maven/KSP/plugin/script/annotation/cinterop/network escape hatch, package-selected toolchain/path/env/channel/install/trust input, or auto-install. Define deterministic macOS/Windows/Linux qualification rules while keeping current Kotlin/Native host evidence UNVERIFIED and making no false platform claim. Preserve frozen releases; no stage/commit/publish/pin; hand off with exhaustive allow/reject matrix and deterministic evidence.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-338c0b, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-338c0b)\nDeveloper run started. Host inventory confirms rhjxtx: no Kotlin/Native distribution on this macOS host (kotlinc-native, konanc, ~/.konan all absent); Kotlin 2.4.10 JVM-backend CLI and OpenJDK 26.0.1 are present. Measured evidence collected under .temp/TASK-260728-168smo/evidence: (1) the shipped Kotlin CLI launcher is a bash wrapper that resolves bash, uname, dirname and java from PATH (4 resolutions under a shim PATH); invoking the fingerprinted JDK java directly with -cp into the Kotlin distribution records 0 PATH resolutions and produces the artifact, exit 0. (2) A bare @-prefixed argument expands as a response file: a build-root file named @inject containing -script plus a .kts source caused the compiler to EXECUTE package code, exit 0. Absolute and ./-prefixed forms of the same path do not expand (exit 1, source entry is not a Kotlin file). (3) JDK_JAVA_OPTIONS and JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS are honoured by the JVM launcher; both notices go to stderr and java --version stdout line 1 stays stable. Task-owned curator-spec worktree created at .temp/TASK-260728-168smo/curator-spec-worktree from clean 57c1f56.\nDeveloper handoff ready for review.\n\nDECISION: Kotlin/Native selected as the v1 artifact model; every Kotlin/JVM shape deferred. Thin JAR, fat JAR (-include-runtime) and jlink/jpackage images all fail decision 0008 section 3 as runtime-bundle: a fat JAR is one file and still not directly loadable by the host program loader, so one file is necessary and not sufficient. GraalVM native-image rejected on four independent grounds (second compile-phase command, third toolchain outside decision 0007 closed set, classpath needs a package manager or a package-controlled member, different backend requiring a different family segment). Identifiers adopted unchanged from decision 0008 section 2: kotlin-native-v1 and kotlin-native-repository-v1. jdk is a REQUIRED companion under a NATIVE model, correcting decision 0007 expectation table, because the Kotlin/Native compiler is JVM-hosted while the produced artifact needs no runtime.\n\nMEASURED (macOS 26.5 / kotlinc-jvm 2.4.10 / OpenJDK 26.0.1; no Kotlin/Native distribution on any reachable host):\n1. @argfile expansion is an ACE channel. A build-root file named @inject containing -script plus a .kts caused the compiler to execute package code, exit 0. Absolute and ./ forms do not expand (exit 1). A missing argfile is a warning with exit 0, so partial mitigation fails silently. Rejection matrix is therefore a closed ALLOW-LIST over name shapes (directories, *.kt, one kotlin-native-module.json, leading-character class excluding dotfiles and @), with absolute-path argv as a measured structural backstop, not as the rule.\n2. Shipped launcher is inadmissible: 4 PATH resolutions (uname, dirname, java -version, java <compile>) plus shebang bash, and it reads six environment channels including KOTLIN_COMPILER which selects the compiler main class. Direct <jdk_root>/bin/java -cp <kotlin_root>/... records 0 PATH resolutions, exit 0, artifact produced. Driver never runs any launcher script, including for the version probe.\n3. Kotlin has no lawful project-metadata file, so the driver mints kotlin-native-module.json {schema_version, kotlin_version}, closed, never passed to the compiler. Stage B classifier is two classes rather than Rust seven; security partition F empty so P1/P2 collapse to C = Upstream.\n4. jdk probe pinned to java --version on stdout: single stream and byte-stable under JDK_JAVA_OPTIONS/JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS injection, both of which were measured to be honoured.\n\nPLATFORM POSITION: platforms and compatibility are EMPTY for both identifiers and both registry entries. No tuple claimed, macOS included. Eight named obligations (K-1..K-8) and a Q1-Q9 acceptance test that requires the control run to fire. macOS is not admitted if any Xcode/usr-bin executable is spawned; Windows forbids cmd/powershell/link.exe/cl.exe/lib.exe/vswhere/VS activation; Linux waits on TASK-260728-1skseh then TASK-260728-3u1nho. Retirement trigger fixed: if no tuple passes Q1-Q9 when TASK-260728-251p01 mints manifest schema 8, both identifiers retire unused and claim schema 4 is minted over six.\n\nREVIEWER ITEMS: (a) decision number 0010 taken because 0009 is claimed concurrently by TASK-260728-12pnm1 and TASK-260728-1jafds; renumbers rather than contests. (b) The narrow reading of decision 0007 section 3 under the JVM-hosted launcher shape (kotlin root contributes no launcher process; primary executable is the companion bin/java) is recorded explicitly as a completion within the section 1.3 mandate, not a widening; if decision 0007 owner rejects it, the consequence is retirement, not a compensating wrapper.\n\nGATES (real exit codes, each standalone): spec validate.py baseline 57c1f56 = 0; spec validate.py task worktree = 1 (expected-red, 3 broken links all in two copied-in in-flight docs, 0 from this task; scoped check over the two authored documents = 0, 4 links); spec unittest = 0; spec go test ./tools/... = 0; curator go build = 0; go vet = 0; go test = 0; gofmt ./cmd ./internal = 0; make check = 2 (expected-red, gofmt stage on four vendored files under .temp/TASK-260720-1zntv0, this task authored 0 Go files). golangci-lint NOT RUN: not installed on this host.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-338c0b, pid=24078, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 1 DIRECTIVE: Independently review the Kotlin/Native artifact-model and driver-pair decision; do not edit producer artifacts. Challenge whether this is truly a host-loadable Kotlin/Native executable model and whether an empty platform matrix plus retirement trigger is an honest, implementable contract rather than a speculative identifier reservation. Verify the manager-owned kotlin-native-module.json surface, direct trusted JDK java invocation, Kotlin root/JDK companion identity, exact process graph, closed source and argv shapes, response-file mitigation, environment scrubbing, artifact extraction, cache/receipt/marker identity, and local/external equivalence. Attempt escape channels through Gradle/Maven/scripts/plugins/KSP/annotation processors/cinterop/network