(Xcode.kt:144). The complete external set for a hello-world is /bin/bash, /usr/bin/xcode-select, /usr/libexec/PlistBuddy, /usr/bin/xcrun, Xcode xcodebuild, Xcode ld, Xcode dsymutil, plus the Xcode SDK as sysroot; with all seven allowed it exits 0. With ignoreXcodeVersionCheck=true and every Apple property overridden to absolute local paths it still spawns /usr/bin/xcrun at AppleConfigurablesImpl.getAbsoluteTargetToolchain(Apple.kt:45). Cause is structural: konan.properties declares the Apple toolchain/sysroot/addon as remote:internal and XcodePartsProvider has only InternalServer (KONAN_USE_INTERNAL_SERVER, repo.labs.intellij.net) and Local (the host Xcode). Second independent ground: the Xcode SDK is an unfingerprinted build input, so two hosts with different Xcode versions alias in the cache key. macos/arm64 and macos/amd64 are therefore permanently unsupported at Protocol 1.0, not pending.\n\nPAIR NOT RETIRED, AND WHY. The reviewer asked for one qualified tuple or retirement now. Neither is available honestly. The measurement proves an APPLE-TARGET failure and shows in the same properties file that targetToolchain/targetSysRoot for mingw_x64 and linux_x64 resolve under KONAN_DATA_DIR/dependencies with no remote:internal and no host SDK. Retiring on macOS evidence would assert a negative about two tuples never measured — the same class of error as claiming them — and retirement is one-way for the whole protocol version because decision 0008 section 2 closes the identifier space. The hard trigger is retained and sharpened: if no tuple passes A1-A9 when TASK-260728-251p01 mints manifest schema 8, both identifiers retire unused.\n\nTWO REVIEW FINDINGS PRODUCED CONTRACT CHANGES, NOT WORDING. (a) The @-response-file defence was stated wrongly: expansion is decided by the argv tokens FIRST CHARACTER, and @/abs/path/file DOES expand. Absolute paths are safe because they start with /, and the driver must never emit an @-prefixed token. (b) The stdlib-only/no-C-interop cla